1790604312.606	**A. Woodblock Printing (Xylography):**
1790604312.606	The most ancient form of mechanical reproduction is woodblock printing. In China, this technique flourished as early as the Tang Dynasty (7th–10th centuries CE). Artisans would carve an entire page—text and image combined—into a single block of wood. This block was then inked and pressed onto paper or fabric. Early examples, such as Buddhist texts from the 8th century, demonstrate sophisticated artistry within this medium.
1790604312.606	
